<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot name="rover" xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">

  <!--
    Chassis geometry (chassis_link + 4x swerve module meshes below) comes
    from an early CAD export (SolidWorks-to-URDF), not the finalized rover
    design — expect these meshes, masses, and joint origins to change again
    as the real chassis design is finished. This replaced the box/cylinder
    placeholder that used to live here (see git history), which was step
    one of two: first wire up Gazebo + ros2_control + Nav2 against
    *something*, then swap in CAD geometry once it existed. This is that
    swap. It is NOT the final step — treat every dimension here as
    provisional until it comes from released-for-manufacture CAD.

    Link/joint names, the ros2_control block, and the Gazebo plugin/material
    wiring were written by hand to match this project's Gazebo Harmonic +
    gz_ros2_control stack; they must stay in sync with
    config/rover_controllers.yaml and
    rover_swerve_controller/swerve_kinematics_node.py if renamed.

    Swerve drivetrain: 4 independently-steerable wheel modules. Each module
    is a steer joint (vertical pivot) with a wheel joint (rolling axis) as
    its child. There's no stock ros2_controllers swerve plugin, so steering
    and wheel-speed commands are driven by two forward_command_controllers
    (see config/rover_controllers.yaml), fed by a custom inverse-kinematics
    node in the rover_swerve_controller package that converts /cmd_vel into
    per-module steer-angle + wheel-speed commands.
  -->

  <xacro:include filename="$(find rover_description)/urdf/materials.xacro" />
  <xacro:include filename="$(find rover_description)/urdf/rover.gazebo" />

  <!--
    REP-103 alignment layer.

    The SolidWorks-to-URDF export gave the chassis body a frame where +x
    points LEFT and +y points to the REAR (see the *_steer_joint origins
    below: "front" modules sit at negative y, "left" modules at positive x).
    ROS conventions (Nav2, slam_toolbox, RViz, teleop) all assume base_link
    is +x forward, +y left, +z up. Driving straight worked but odometry came
    out with the axes swapped, and Nav2 would have driven the rover sideways
    toward goals.

    Fix: base_link is a new REP-103-compliant root. chassis_link is the raw
    CAD body, mounted on base_link through a fixed +90 deg yaw so its "+x =
    left" axis lands on base_link's +y. Everything CAD-derived (meshes,
    swerve modules) hangs off chassis_link and is untouched; everything ROS
    talks to (odom, TF, sensors) hangs off base_link. If the finalized CAD
    is ever re-exported with a corrected coordinate system, delete this
    layer and rename chassis_link back to base_link.

    base_link gets a token inertial only because gz-sim requires the model's
    root (canonical) link to have one; the real 595 kg is on chassis_link
    and gets lumped in across the fixed joint.
  -->
  <link name="base_link">
    <inertial>
      <mass value="0.001"/>
      <inertia ixx="1e-6" ixy="0" ixz="0" iyy="1e-6" iyz="0" izz="1e-6"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <joint name="base_link_to_chassis" type="fixed">
    <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 1.5708"/>
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="chassis_link"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="chassis_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="1.7662172446492366e-08 0.04237215152825712 0.09216107589120397" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="595.1849542563896"/>
      <inertia ixx="19.500193" iyy="39.83973" izz="55.970633" ixy="1e-06" iyz="-0.807843" ixz="0.0"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/base_link.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/base_link.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <link name="front_left_wheel_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.0507999999999999 -1.1102230246251565e-16 5.551115123125783e-17" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="25.864295489856012"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.133493" iyy="0.088995" izz="0.088995" ixy="-0.0" iyz="0.0" ixz="0.0"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.3556 0.3175 0.1905" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/wheel1_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="-0.3556 0.3175 0.1905" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/wheel1_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <link name="rear_left_wheel_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.050799999999999956 1.1102230246251565e-16 3.885780586188048e-16" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="25.864295489856012"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.133493" iyy="0.088995" izz="0.088995" ixy="0.0" iyz="0.0" ixz="0.0"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.3556 -0.2921 0.1905" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/wheel3_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="-0.3556 -0.2921 0.1905" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/wheel3_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <link name="front_right_wheel_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.050799999999999845 -3.6637359812630166e-15 -2.7755575615628914e-16" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="25.864295489856012"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.133493" iyy="0.088995" izz="0.088995" ixy="-0.0" iyz="-0.0" ixz="0.0"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0.3556 0.3175 0.1905" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/wheel2_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.3556 0.3175 0.1905" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/wheel2_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <link name="rear_right_wheel_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.05080000000000029 -3.7192471324942744e-15 1.6653345369377348e-16" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="25.864295489856012"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.133493" iyy="0.088995" izz="0.088995" ixy="0.0" iyz="0.0" ixz="0.0"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0.3556 -0.2921 0.1905" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/wheel4_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.3556 -0.2921 0.1905" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/wheel4_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <link name="front_left_steer_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.004588209054589121 -1.1102230246251565e-16 -0.0951512261261479" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="11.71442300300121"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.072711" iyy="0.074344" izz="0.018661" ixy="0.0" iyz="-0.0" ixz="-0.013033"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.3556 0.3175 -0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/mount1_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="-0.3556 0.3175 -0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/mount1_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <link name="front_right_steer_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.00458820905458901 5.551115123125783e-17 -0.09515122612614813" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="11.714423003001206"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.072711" iyy="0.074344" izz="0.018661" ixy="0.0" iyz="0.0" ixz="0.013033"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0.3556 0.3175 -0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/mount2_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.3556 0.3175 -0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/mount2_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <link name="rear_left_steer_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.00458820905458901 1.1102230246251565e-16 -0.09515122612614782" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="11.71442300300121"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.072711" iyy="0.074344" izz="0.018661" ixy="0.0" iyz="0.0" ixz="-0.013033"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.3556 -0.2921 -0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/mount3_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="-0.3556 -0.2921 -0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/mount3_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <link name="rear_right_steer_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.004588209054588566 -5.551115123125783e-17 -0.09515122612614793" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="11.71442300300121"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.072711" iyy="0.074344" izz="0.018661" ixy="0.0" iyz="0.0" ixz="0.013033"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0.3556 -0.2921 -0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/mount4_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.3556 -0.2921 -0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="file://$(find rover_description)/meshes/mount4_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <joint name="front_left_wheel_joint" type="continuous">
    <origin xyz="0.0 0.0 -0.2159" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <parent link="front_left_steer_link"/>
    <child link="front_left_wheel_link"/>
    <axis xyz="1.0 0.0 0.0"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="rear_left_wheel_joint" type="continuous">
    <origin xyz="0.0 0.0 -0.2159" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <parent link="rear_left_steer_link"/>
    <child link="rear_left_wheel_link"/>
    <axis xyz="1.0 0.0 0.0"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="front_right_wheel_joint" type="continuous">
    <origin xyz="0.0 0.0 -0.2159" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <parent link="front_right_steer_link"/>
    <child link="front_right_wheel_link"/>
    <axis xyz="1.0 0.0 0.0"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="rear_right_wheel_joint" type="continuous">
    <origin xyz="0.0 0.0 -0.2159" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <parent link="rear_right_steer_link"/>
    <child link="rear_right_wheel_link"/>
    <axis xyz="1.0 0.0 0.0"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="front_left_steer_joint" type="continuous">
    <origin xyz="0.3556 -0.3175 0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <parent link="chassis_link"/>
    <child link="front_left_steer_link"/>
    <axis xyz="0.0 0.0 1.0"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="front_right_steer_joint" type="continuous">
    <origin xyz="-0.3556 -0.3175 0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <parent link="chassis_link"/>
    <child link="front_right_steer_link"/>
    <axis xyz="0.0 0.0 1.0"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="rear_left_steer_joint" type="continuous">
    <origin xyz="0.3556 0.2921 0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <parent link="chassis_link"/>
    <child link="rear_left_steer_link"/>
    <axis xyz="0.0 0.0 1.0"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="rear_right_steer_joint" type="continuous">
    <origin xyz="-0.3556 0.2921 0.0254" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <parent link="chassis_link"/>
    <child link="rear_right_steer_link"/>
    <axis xyz="0.0 0.0 1.0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- Sensor mount points are placeholders (not yet taken from real CAD
       mount locations) — revisit once the chassis design settles. These
       hang off base_link (not chassis_link) on purpose, so their frames
       are REP-103 aligned: lidar 0 deg and camera +x both point at the
       rover's true forward. -->
  <joint name="lidar_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="lidar_link"/>
    <origin xyz="0 0 0.25" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="lidar_link">
    <visual>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.04" length="0.06"/></geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.04" length="0.06"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <mass value="0.2"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.0001" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0" iyy="0.0001" iyz="0.0" izz="0.0001"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <!-- Frame reserved for the stereo camera; no sensor plugin yet — lidar-based
       slam_toolbox is the near-term priority per CLAUDE.md's SLAM go/no-go plan. -->
  <joint name="camera_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="camera_link"/>
    <origin xyz="0.35 0 0.1" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="camera_link">
    <visual>
      <geometry><box size="0.03 0.09 0.03"/></geometry>
      <material name="silver"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <geometry><box size="0.03 0.09 0.03"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <mass value="0.1"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.00005" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0" iyy="0.00005" iyz="0.0" izz="0.00005"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <xacro:macro name="steer_ros2_control" params="prefix">
    <joint name="${prefix}_steer_joint">
      <command_interface name="position"/>
      <state_interface name="position"/>
      <state_interface name="velocity"/>
    </joint>
  </xacro:macro>

  <xacro:macro name="wheel_ros2_control" params="prefix">
    <joint name="${prefix}_wheel_joint">
      <command_interface name="velocity"/>
      <state_interface name="velocity"/>
      <state_interface name="position"/>
    </joint>
  </xacro:macro>

  <ros2_control name="gz_ros2_control_system" type="system">
    <hardware>
      <plugin>gz_ros2_control/GazeboSimSystem</plugin>
    </hardware>
    <xacro:steer_ros2_control prefix="front_left"/>
    <xacro:wheel_ros2_control prefix="front_left"/>
    <xacro:steer_ros2_control prefix="front_right"/>
    <xacro:wheel_ros2_control prefix="front_right"/>
    <xacro:steer_ros2_control prefix="rear_left"/>
    <xacro:wheel_ros2_control prefix="rear_left"/>
    <xacro:steer_ros2_control prefix="rear_right"/>
    <xacro:wheel_ros2_control prefix="rear_right"/>
  </ros2_control>

  <gazebo>
    <plugin filename="gz_ros2_control-system" name="gz_ros2_control::GazeboSimROS2ControlPlugin">
      <parameters>$(find rover_description)/config/rover_controllers.yaml</parameters>
    </plugin>
  </gazebo>

  <!-- Ground-truth odometry: publishes the odom->base_link transform and an
       Odometry message straight from Gazebo's physics state, i.e. zero drift.
       This is deliberately the cheap version to unblock slam_toolbox / Nav2
       bring-up (a continuous odom->base_link TF is a hard requirement for
       both). Replace later with real wheel odometry integrated from the
       swerve module joint states, which will have the drift SLAM exists to
       correct. dimensions=2 matches the planar sim world and the 2D
       slam_toolbox that consumes this. -->
  <gazebo>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-odometry-publisher-system"
            name="gz::sim::systems::OdometryPublisher">
      <dimensions>2</dimensions>
      <odom_frame>odom</odom_frame>
      <robot_base_frame>base_link</robot_base_frame>
      <odom_publish_frequency>50</odom_publish_frequency>
      <!-- Leading slash keeps these as absolute gz topic names, so Gazebo
           does NOT scope them as /model/rover/... . The gz_bridge in
           gazebo.launch.py bridges these exact names into ROS. -->
      <odom_topic>/odom</odom_topic>
      <tf_topic>/odom_tf</tf_topic>
    </plugin>
  </gazebo>

  <gazebo reference="lidar_link">
    <sensor name="lidar" type="gpu_lidar">
      <topic>scan</topic>
      <update_rate>10</update_rate>
      <!-- Without this, Gazebo stamps /scan with a scoped sensor name like
           "rover/.../lidar" that has no entry in the TF tree
           (robot_state_publisher only publishes "lidar_link"), so
           slam_toolbox and RViz would silently drop every scan. VERIFY on
           the next run that /scan's header.frame_id is exactly
           "lidar_link". -->
      <gz_frame_id>lidar_link</gz_frame_id>
      <ray>
        <scan>
          <horizontal>
            <samples>360</samples>
            <min_angle>-3.14159</min_angle>
            <max_angle>3.14159</max_angle>
          </horizontal>
        </scan>
        <range>
          <min>0.1</min>
          <max>30.0</max>
        </range>
      </ray>
    </sensor>
  </gazebo>

</robot>
